Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: resize query buffers with a buffer layout

Delayed query allocations are PIPE_BUFFER / R8_UNORM, initially width zero.
After setting width0, update the buffer layout and allocate its requested byte
size, as resource creation does. Image slice setup sees the old layout width
and can allocate a BO too small for per-tile query samples on A3xx.
Observed with GL_ANY_SAMPLES_PASSED at 1280x800: OUT_RELOC offset exceeds BO.
Separate correctness fix; not established as a cause of the GUI FPS deficit.
Bounded true/empty occlusion query checks passed; the retained correctness
scope and limits are documented in Porting Notes/mesa.md.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,10 @@
    assert(prsc->bind == PIPE_BIND_QUERY_BUFFER);
 
    prsc->width0 = sz;
-   realloc_bo(rsc, fd_screen(prsc->screen)->setup_slices(rsc));
+   /* Query resources are buffers; image slice setup still sees the old
+    * zero-width layout and can underallocate multi-tile query storage. */
+   fdl_layout_buffer(&rsc->layout, sz);
+   realloc_bo(rsc, sz);
 }
 
 static void
